    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d679">

                <pb facs="0730" n="472" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg472"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/1343a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-07-14T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 14, 1915, 5 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1848. In order to avoid any misunderstanding as to attitude of Government of
                    United States in regard to prize court proceedings in cases involving American
                    interests, inform British Government that in view of differences which are
                    understood to exist between the two Governments as to the principles of law
                    applicable in these cases, the Government of the United States desires to make
                    clear to the British Government that in so far as the interests of American
                    citizens are concerned, it will insist upon their rights under the hitherto
                    established principles and rules of international law governing neutral trade in
                    time of war, without modification or limitation by orders in council or other
                    municipal legislation by Great Britain, and it will not recognize the validity
                    of proceedings taken in prize court under restraints imposed by British
                    municipal law in derogation of their rights.</p>
                <p>Inform Urion<anchor n="1" xml:id="d679-f1"/> and report any suggestions by
                    him.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d679-f1" n="1" xml:id="d679-f1-content">
                <p>Attorney for the American packers. See telegrams from the Ambassador, May 21, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg405">p. 405</ref>, and July
                    17, <hi rendition="#italic">post</hi>, <ref target="#pg474">p. 474</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
